WEBVTT

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.200
Sou-kun, what should we do?

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.460
Right, well... Um...

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.000
Sou...

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.540
What?

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.920
Isn't there anything you can remember?

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.380
About your family? Or your school?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.510
Touch the box...

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.180
What?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.100
Touch... the box...

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.100
The box?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:42.980
More like, this screams of something illicit.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.980
It's okay. You can come in.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.230
I'm so glad we had your uniform, Airi-chan.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.570
I keep it on hand just for emergencies like these.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.860
Not for when you go on a rampage?

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.070
No!

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.030
Oh! It suits you!

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:02.250
What?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.710
She's looking at me...

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:10.210
Tell me, Yui-san.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.590
Do you know what this is?

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.760
I see. It's something we've been studying for some time now.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.470
I'll make you a cup of steamed milk to help you sleep well tonight.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.400
Touch the box...

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.750
<i>And I remember.</i>

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.210
<i>I remember everything that has happened.</i>

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.820
How many times has it been for me since then?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.940
Y-Yui-chan, where are we going?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.990
Please, just come! There's no time for questions!

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.820
W-Wait, Yui-chan.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:42.570
Ow!

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.490
Your leg injury...

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.530
I-It's not a big deal...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.260
Kaori-san?!

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.140
No way...

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.600
We have to get help!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.600
Kaori-san?!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:14.810
Wait!

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.740
<i>The more I tried to circumvent the accident,</i>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.990
<i>the more horrific the results became.</i>

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.040
<i>It was like I was being warned.</i>

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.080
Furukawa-san?

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:37.170
What are you doing?

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.000
Sou—

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.500
A-Akiyama-san...

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.090
It's only morning,
and you're already skipping class?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.880
I wanted to get some sunlight.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.510
You sound like an old woman.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.980
<i>Sou, I want to ask you for your help.</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.230
<i>I want to tell you everything right this minute.</i>

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.900
Something the matter?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.650
Huh? Not at all...

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.940
Oh?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.650
But man, I really wish I could skip too.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.200
<i>But I cannot do that.</i>

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.370
They said there's been another case.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.080
That falling asleep thing?
A taxi driver, wasn't it?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.620
Talk about scary, right?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.710
I heard there's been a couple cases here at the academy, too.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.210
Have you heard about that, Furukawa-san?

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.260
Yes. Or at least the rumors.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.220
The Uchihama syndrome...

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.220
A mysterious phenomenon occurring frequently here, around Uchihama.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:34.100
With no prior warning,
people fall into a deep sleep,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.390
never to awaken again.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.730
A mysterious illness.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.230
We'll be counting on you to take care of it.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.900
Before this commotion gets even bigger.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.370
What are we going to do about this ghost investigation thing?

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.830
It sounds like fun!

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.540
This isn't fun at all.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.410
"Yuurei"?

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:54.870
That's "ghost"!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:55.450
<i>In truth, the ghosts are me.</i>

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.040
Oh!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.370
Let's start by questioning eyewitnesses and investigating its known locations.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.460
<i>To be precise,</i>

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.670
<i>they are afterimages that have arisen as a result of my repeatedly living the same period of time.</i>

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.460
What a pain.
<i>they are afterimages that have arisen as a result of my repeatedly living the same period of time.</i>

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.800
I guess I'll... hold down the fort here?

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.340
<i>My overlapping selves in other timelines</i>

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.090
<i>are being projected on this one due to quantum oscillations.</i>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.550
Oh no, you're not! You're coming too, Kaori!

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:16.890
<i>And that was causing another serious problem.</i>

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.150
<i>In one timeline...</i>

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.860
It's not here.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:23.480
What'll I do?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.450
Huh?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.320
What is this?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.580
What's going on? Is this an image?

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.580
<i>The moment she came into contact with my shadow...</i>

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:46.880
<i>To my knowledge, the Azuma Yaeko in that timeline never woke up.</i>

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.050
<i>We can surmise that, due to the effects of the quantum oscillations,</i>

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:53.800
<i>her consciousness was likely transported to some other timeline.</i>

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.890
I heard there's been another case of
Uchihama syndrome in the neighborhood.

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.560
It's scary, isn't it?

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.770
I hope they at least figure out what's causing it.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.980
Maybe it's the work of the ghost.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.280
H-Hey, stop that, Sou-kun!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.280
<i>The Uchihama syndrome...
H-Hey, stop that, Sou-kun!</i>

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:13.070
<i>There are three kinds of people who are especially susceptible to the quantum oscillations.</i>

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.500
<i>Those who come into
direct contact with my shadow.</i>

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.910
<i>Those whose wavelengths just happen to become synchronized.</i>

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.960
<i>And those who interfere
with my trying to change the future.</i>

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.460
<i>Those people have a higher probability of succumbing to the syndrome.</i>

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.720
Okay, then. We'll decide our partners for the ghost investigation.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.430
I'll catch that Japanese ghost!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.600
<i>Both the ghost sightings
and cases of Uchihama syndrome</i>

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.270
<i>are increasing in frequency
with every trip I take back in time.</i>

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.690
<i>If a member of our group were to succumb to this sleep...</i>

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.150
<i>the continuity of time would be lost.</i>

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.280
<i>I would not be created in the future,</i>

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.370
<i>and my very existence would be lost...</i>

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.790
<i>along with any chance of my being able to prevent Kaori-san's accident.</i>

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.790
Okay, then... Who am I going with?

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.630
<i>A smile for Sou...</i>

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.180
I am with Akiyama-san.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:15.720
O-Okay, best of luck to us.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.720
Then I'm with Kaori.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.480
We've apparently gotten the most sightings reported from around here.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.770
They say that other things happen as well,

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.230
like stuff suddenly tumbling down and windows rattling, but...

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.900
There's nothing in particular here.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:32.990
No, there is not.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.990
<i>The place I was transported to.</i>

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:41.290
<i>The effects of the quantum oscillations must still linger...</i>

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.170
Are you the kind that's scared of ghosts and things?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.290
N-Not particularly...

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.500
Yeah, right?

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.420
Being afraid of ghosts at our age is a bit much.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:57.390
What's that sound?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.020
Furukawa!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.640
Owowow!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.350
S-Sou?!

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.060
Y-You okay?

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.650
Injured... Are you injured?!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.320
I'm fine. Never mind that...

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.280
You just called me by my first name, didn't you?

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:15.820
What?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.740
Oh, pardon me. I did not mean to.

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.370
Actually, you called me "Sou" when we first met, too.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.950
What was that sound?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:24.910
Oh dear, you sure did a number on this place.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.120
Are you okay?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.130
Y-Yes.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.470
All right, we're making good progress preparing for the school festival,

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.140
so that just leaves the ghost that we were asked to investigate...

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.220
Hasekura-san, come right away.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:43.850
It's the Judo Club and the Karate Club!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.350
Shut up!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.070
Yui-chan!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.270
Furukawa!

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.480
Kaori!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.280
You punks!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.540
<i>By taking injuries myself,
I can circumvent Kaori-san suffering them.</i>

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.960
<i>This has already been proven
in an alternate timeline.</i>

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.630
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry, Yui-chan.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.420
Oh no, I am just glad that you
are all right, Sasaki-san.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.420
Yui-chan...

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.180
<i>But anything more is dangerous.</i>

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:24.930
<i>I stand against the chains of fate,
which correct time.</i>

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.270
<i>And their power is great.</i>

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:28.850
Why?!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.900
Yui-chan, what is this for?!

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.190
Open the door!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:33.980
I will explain the reason later.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.940
Please stay in there for just a little while!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.490
Yui-chan! Huh?

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:38.950
Wh-What?

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.160
What in the world is this?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:49.250
Kaori-san!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:52.500
<i>If I try to directly limit Kaori-san's movements,</i>

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:55.670
<i>it gives rise to accidents
that no one could have foreseen.</i>

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:02.340
Wow, it's made pretty well.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.270
<i>I have to be careful in how I affect the events that play out.</i>

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:10.850
<i>The accident must be circumvented by interfering as little as possible.</i>

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:15.730
<i>I have slowly discovered what is possible and what is not</i>

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:19.400
<i>through trial and error
over many repetitions of the timeline.</i>

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.780
<i>And this time, surely...</i>

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.950
Does it still hurt?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.080
Not so much.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.750
I suppose this should bring
the whole ghost incident to a close.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:32.080
I swear! First the Judo Club,
and then the Film Society...

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.460
They get up to the most worthless things!

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:36.630
I wanted to see the Japanese ghost!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.760
<i>My ever-increasing shadows...</i>

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.380
<i>The Uchihama syndrome...</i>

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:47.680
<i>Eventually, it will surely halt
my very ability to travel back in time.</i>

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>I have to save Kaori-san
before that happens.</i>

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.620
<i>For Sou's smile as well.</i>

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:08.240
What's wrong, Furukawa?

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:09.080
Does it hurt?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.710
Oh, no, it is not a problem.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.840
<i>If I save Kaori-san, the future will change.</i>

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.380
<i>When that happens, my own existence...</i>

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:29.350
<i>But that is the purpose for which I am here.</i>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.190
Hey, Sou-kun.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:39.480
About Yui-chan... How do you feel about her?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.070
What?

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.240
H-How do I feel?

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.530
"Symptom" here refers to a "sign."

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.990
And "boldness" means "to be daring."

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.040
In other words, the sign of true love in a man is...

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.620
<i>Back then, why did she...</i>

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.960
Wh-What the...

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.750
H-How am I supposed to answer just like that?

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.500
Do you love Yui-chan?

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:04.220
Wh-Why?! I've only just met Furukawa, and...

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.470
Wh-Why are you asking me in the first place?

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.560
Sorry. It was just a little something I wanted to ask.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.350
Kaori?

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:22.610
<i>But I couldn't flat out deny it
when she asked about Furukawa...</i>

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:25.610
<i>How </i>do<i> I really feel?</i>

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:30.700
Kaori-san is absent?

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.870
Yeah, she's apparently not feeling well.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:34.710
Not feeling well?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.210
<i>Why? Nothing like this has happened before...</i>

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.920
Did you need something from Kaori?

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:42.210
What caused this?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.130
Is there nothing that you can think of?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.090
The cause?

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.890
I don't... really know.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:55.850
I see.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.940
No, but it doesn't mean that's what caused...

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:01.770
Furukawa?!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:05.240
Hey, Sou! How's it going with the camera?

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:06.780
Huh? Uh, Sou?!

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.160
Furukawa, where are you going?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.830
To Kaori-san's home.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:12.580
Why?

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.790
Kaori-san is not supposed to be absent on this day.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.370
Huh?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.420
There has to be some reason.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.750
A reason for Kaori-san to be absent.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:21.540
Hey!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.050
Is there some problem if Kaori doesn't come?

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.220
What? That is...

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:33.470
Sh-She is a fellow member
of the Astronomy Club, after all.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:37.980
All right.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.770
I'll bring Kaori tomorrow for sure.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:48.700
Hello?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.280
How are you feeling?

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:53.370
You were... worried about me?

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.660
Well, sure. And it's not just me.

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.290
Everyone else is worried too, so...

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.920
Is there anything you want me
to pick up for you on the way home?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.550
Um... Custard pudding, then.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.050
Got it.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.930
I'm okay now. Let the others know
I'll be in tomorrow.

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.050
Okay, later.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.020
Are you feeling all right now?

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:24.940
Yeah. I'm sorry for worrying everyone.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:27.030
Yui-chan, is your leg okay now?

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.690
Oh, yes, it is fine.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:29.740
I'm glad.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.780
I thought you'd had another fight
with Sou or something.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.070
Not really.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.410
It wasn't exactly like that.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:35.950
Um...

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.710
How about we all take a picture
with this camera?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:42.540
Huh? What's this all of a sudden?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.000
How unusual, coming from you.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.420
I don't see why not.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.300
I want to try out this
analog camera thing anyway.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.670
Yes, of course.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.890
Then shall we make the most of this
and take it outside?

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:56.050
Mm, that's the spirit that
makes us the Astronomy Club.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:15:59.890
Okay...

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:07.020
Did that just take a picture?

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:08.070
P-Probably...

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.070
<i>If only these times could go on forever.</i>

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.070
Yui-chan...

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.570
I want to talk to you for a bit.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.370
S-Stop the hell right there!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.580
Yo.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:20.450
Outta the way!
Hello.

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:21.040
Outta the way!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:21.870
Huh?

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.630
Hasekura-san...

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.840
Um, Kao—

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.090
I mean, Sasaki-san.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.720
Kaori's fine. What is it?

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:43.020
You said you wanted to talk to me earlier.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.770
Y-Yeah, so...

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.270
Good grief.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.400
You saved me by being there, Nagisa-san.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.280
It was just a bit of fun.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:55.490
Oh, we can do this some other time.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.280
Okay.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.450
A badge that says you're a member of the Astronomy Club.

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:05.500
This is coming a little late, but...

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.340
We all have one.

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.720
Thank you very much.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:22.770
Furukawa-san!

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.100
Yes?

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.020
Did something good happen?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.520
Why do you ask?

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:33.650
Well, I'm a Furukawa-nist, and I sensed an "I'm happy" aura, if you will...

00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.360
What does that even mean?

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.700
Karin, come here for a sec!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.530
Hm? Okay!

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:42.580
<i>The things that happened
have not changed by much.</i>

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:47.540
<i>Which is why I thought that we were on the same time continuity as ever.</i>

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:49.880
<i>But...</i>

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:01.050
Oh, Yui-chan. The cookies are done.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.560
Where is Hasekura-san?

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.600
She went to take a freshly
baked batch to the other two.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.100
What do you think?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.650
It is delicious.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.610
Glad to hear it.

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.780
Here's the thing, Yui-chan...

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:23.120
I-It's about Sou-kun. Do you... love him?

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.080
What?

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:31.880
I want to know how you honestly feel.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.590
My feelings for Akiyama-san...

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.600
I...

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:45.430
I asked Sou-kun the other day.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.600
About how he feels about you.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.060
What?

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:52.150
He wouldn't give me a straight answer,

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.320
but I had a suspicion that he loves you.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:03.120
You know, I love Sou-kun too.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.160
I always have.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.000
I thought about giving up on him at one point,

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:13.420
but I can't lie to myself about how I feel.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.380
Because, in the end, I really do love him.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.010
Kaori-san...

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.220
I'm sorry to spring this on you.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:24.300
That's not it! If that is the case, then what am I doing here?!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:24.890
What?

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.600
Yui-chan?

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:31.980
Oh!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.400
Yui-chan?!

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.440
Whoa! Yui?!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.110
Wait, Yui-chan!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.740
Did something happen?

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.610
Sou-kun!

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.790
<i>How could this have happened?</i>

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.130
<i>What should I...</i>

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:01.220
Furukawa!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:07.140
Yui!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.810
Why did you run away?

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.480
Did something happen between you and Kaori?

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:14.060
Please love her back!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:14.560
What?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:18.320
Please return Kaori-san's love for you!

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:20.740
Wh-What the...

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.280
Why Kaori?

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:30.080
Because, Sou, for you, that is the best...

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.210
The best...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:35.790
It doesn't matter who I fall in love with, does it?

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:38.630
You can't.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:42.300
Whether that's Kaori, or Airi, or Nagisa-san.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:44.430
You can't.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:48.010
Or even you, Yui.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.100
You cannot.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.270
Why not?!

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.440
It will change things.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:01.610
It will change <i>everything</i>.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.950
You cannot do this!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:04.450
Yui?

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.950
Because I will be going away soon!

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.700
G-Going away? What do you mean?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.210
Like, you're transferring away somewhere?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.210
Explain it to me properly!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.840
I cannot tell you right now.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.880
But I can only be here for a little while longer.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.430
Please, Sou.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.970
I am begging you to think of Kaori-san.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:31.770
Tell me why.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.480
If you do not...

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:41.400
You...

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.440
You will not find happiness!

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.530
What do you mean by that?

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.240
You're not making any sense.

00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:26.880
The future that Sou desires...

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:27.960
Did something happen between you and Yui-chan?

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:29.340
There is a favor I would like to ask of you.

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:30.470
There's something I have to say.

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:31.590
Why is it Yui?

00:23:31.590 --> 00:23:33.600
Are you okay with that, Yui-chan?

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.060
Goodbye.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:39.980
Episode eleven: "I'll See You Again Tomorrow, Right?"
